    "remoteAccess": {
      "type": "role-based-vpn",
      "note": "Role-based IKEv2 VPN on the Istanbul firewall with a certificate, MFA and directory groups: admins reach network management VLANs, developers reach Git and CI/CD, staff reach ERP. No SSH from the internet. Separately, IPsec links all sites with Istanbul as VPN hub; every site accepts IPsec from the others as common rule B."
    },
    "monitoring": {
      "siem": "FortiAnalyzer and SIEM for logs and correlation, Prometheus + Grafana for health and capacity, NetFlow/IPFIX for flows, SOAR limited to alerts, failover to backup link and temporary single-IP quarantine. Logs stay online for 90 days and in the archive for 2 years; Law 5651 logs are signed daily with a timestamp; London logs are kept separately. Cloudflare WAF events reach the SIEM through Logpush.",
      "owner": "NOC (5 operators) and SOC (5 Tier 1, 3 Tier 2) staffed in three shifts from Istanbul with Ankara as backup; firewall engineers (3) change rules only with a ticket and a second approver; 2 incident managers; 2 security manager/DPO roles for KVKK and UK-GDPR. Firewall engineers patch FortiOS, FortiManager and FortiAnalyzer in a monthly window, and within 72 hours for a vulnerability under active exploitation, following Fortinet PSIRT advisories.",
      "alertSink": "Ticket system fed by SIEM (SOC) and Prometheus (NOC); critical alerts get a 15-minute first response.",
      "appVsSecurity": "NOC watches links, VPN, HA and capacity; SOC watches attacks; neither can change permanent rules, which belong to the firewall engineers."
    },
